# Local working area: acceptance evidence, release tarballs, client
# transcripts, and scratch copies of node_modules. Never shipped, and it
# contains user paths and conversation content that must not be published.
.dispatch/

# Editor / OS noise
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.idea/
.vscode/

# dist/ IS committed on purpose.
#
# codeg launches agents from a distribution spec, and the JS channel for that is
# `npx` — which is what makes this work on someone else's machine without them
# editing paths. That means the package has to run after a plain `npx <repo>`
# install, and npm installs do NOT run `prepare` for git dependencies over
# https… except when they do. Rather than depend on that, the built output is
# checked in: it is 430 KB of plain ESM, it is what actually runs, and its
# presence removes an entire class of "works on my machine" failures.
#
# Rebuild before committing with:  npm run build && npm run verify
